@tradition open-door
// Open door (0.60.7): end-of-shift tea on Wednesdays at the Works tea corner, where the Chief sits with whoever's
// there. It opens at 16:40; Works crew still on shift come straight from it (after-shift), Calder too.
k: 445
title: Open door
when: weekly wednesday
at: 16:40-18:00
min: 15
after-shift: yes
where: 5 room Tea corner: lounge-seat
where: 5 room Works bay: work:works, free
hold: 1
who: calder always, works 40%, tea-break 25%, everyone 4%
anim: calder talk, everyone drink
host: calder
from: calder

== mail
- Open door tomorrow at the tea corner from {time}. Bring a question, a gripe, or just a mug. I'll be there.

== ask
- Open door after shift. The Chief actually listens. Go on.   #warm
- Calder's tea corner at end of shift. Bring the question you've been saving.
- Open door today. Tea, biscuits, and the Chief with her boots off.   #funny

== here
- Ask her anything. She'll tell you straight.
- More tea? The pot's still hot.
- She fixed my rota in two minutes. Two.   #funny

== thanks
- You sit down at the tea corner with Chief Calder. She asks how your week is going, and waits for the real answer.   #warm

== chatter
- Open door's the only meeting I don't mind.   #funny
- I asked the Chief about the coolant pumps at open door. She drew me a diagram on a napkin.
